# Shell scripts must be LF in the repository regardless of contributor platform.
#
# get.sh and deploy/install.sh are fetched over HTTP and piped straight into sh
# on Linux nodes. A CRLF copy fails there with an obscure error — the shebang
# resolves to "/usr/bin/env sh\r", which does not exist. Today these files are
# LF only because core.autocrlf happened to normalise them on the machines they
# were committed from; this makes it a property of the repository instead.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: CRLF breaks line continuations and here-docs in RUN steps.
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
